    "result_text": "All tests pass. `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` event emitted to the `AUDIT` log, alongside the existing human-readable audit line. The work is split by responsibility rather than piled into the existing audit class:\n\n- **`util/PrimaryIdentifier.java`** \u2014 single source of truth for the owner's *current* primary identifier. It returns the `customerCode` today; when the identity is unified into a memberId, only this one method changes and the event automatically carries the memberId. This directly satisfies the spec's forward-looking requirement.\n\n- **`rest/event/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 an immutable `record` value object holding `{seq, ownerId, primaryIdentifier, membershipLevel}` plus the `OWNER_CREATED` type constant. Its `toJson()` renders the compact JSON in the documented field order, serializing the identifier under the `customerCode` key (with proper string escaping and bare `null` for absent values).\n\n- **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 a new pipeline step (single responsibility: emit the structured event). It computes the membership level by reusing the existing `MembershipPoints`/`MembershipLevel` helpers, takes the next value from a process-wide `AtomicLong` so `seq` is monotonically increasing across all creates, and logs the JSON via the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `auditEvent` step in after the existing `audit` step (both under `govern: [ transaction ]`), before `respond`.\n\nThe existing `AuditOwnerCreated` human-readable line is left untouched, so both outputs now appear:\n```\nINFO AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...\nINFO AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` and the full suite are green.",
